LOCUS       mg1655_thrL_xref         300 bp    DNA     linear   SYN 29-APR-2026
DEFINITION  Synthetic linear region modeled after the E. coli K-12 MG1655
            thrL operon start. Carries NCBI-style /db_xref annotations to
            exercise the multi-value qualifier parser.
ACCESSION   mg1655_thrL_multi_xref
VERSION     mg1655_thrL_multi_xref
COMMENT     regression fixture. The forward-strand CDS at 1..66 is the
            thrL coding region as annotated in NCBI U00096.3 (MG1655 reference
            genome), reduced to its qualifier surface. The four /db_xref lines
            are the actual cross-references on the live thrL annotation
            (UniProt, ASAP, EcoCyc, EcoGene); the parser previously kept only
            the last entry. The complement-strand CDS at 100..165 is hand-
            authored to give the round-trip test a second multi-xref feature
            and to verify that ordering is preserved per-feature, not globally.
            Singleton qualifiers (/gene, /locus_tag, /protein_id, /translation)
            should parse to length-1 arrays. The 300 bp ORIGIN sequence is
            seeded ACGT filler — biological identity does not matter for the
            qualifier-preservation tests this fixture exists to support.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     CDS             1..66
                     /label="thrL"
                     /gene="thrL"
                     /locus_tag="b0001"
                     /protein_id="AAC73112.1"
                     /codon_start="1"
                     /transl_table="11"
                     /translation="MKRISTTITTTITITTGNGAG"
                     /db_xref="UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot:P0AD86"
                     /db_xref="ASAP:ABE-0000006"
                     /db_xref="ECOCYC:EG10998"
                     /db_xref="EcoGene:EG10998"
     CDS             complement(100..165)
                     /label="rev_dual_xref"
                     /gene="rev_dual_xref"
                     /codon_start="1"
                     /transl_table="11"
                     /translation="MAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA"
                     /db_xref="UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot:P00000"
                     /db_xref="GeneID:99999"
ORIGIN
        1 atgaaacgca ttagcaccac cattaccacc accatcacca ttaccacagg taacggtgcg
       61 ggctgacgcg tacaggaaac acagaaaaaa gcccgcacct gacagtgcgg gctttttttt
      121 tcgaccaaag gtaacgaggt aacaaccatg cgagtgttga agttcggcgg tacatcagtg
      181 gcaaatgcag aacgttttct gcgtgttgcc gatattctgg aaagcaatgc caggcaggat
      241 gtttacctta tcggtgaaaa actaagacac caacgaagaa atgcgaccaa gccatatcca
